## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: A user complains they are getting an administrator prompt when trying to connect to a network printer. What caused this?
A1: The "PrintNightmare" security patch. By default, standard users cannot install print drivers. The IT department must configure the "Point and Print Restrictions" Group Policy to explicitly trust the print server.

Q2: Why did we link the PrintNightmare bypass GPO to the Domain root, but link the Printer Deployment GPO to the HR OU?
A2: The PrintNightmare bypass modifies the registry of the local computer hardware (Computer Configuration) to allow driver installations, so it must hit the computer objects. The Printer Deployment is targeted at specific employees (User Configuration), so it should only apply to the HR OU.